							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">I doubt there will ever be any game as popular as EQ. It was the first online game that managed to captivate thousands of people. It was new and exciting. All games that follow will be compared to EQ, willingly or not. The &#039;virgin&#039; feeling that a lot of people got when starting EQ will not come again no matter what other online game they play. Sure a game like WoW might be fun for a while but in the end I think people will get bored with it pretty fast. Not everyone of course but many. In my opinion the only thing that will keep someone playing any online game for lenghts of time is if they have established a solid friendbase. Many people leave one game together to try something new which often extends the amount of time someone is willing to stay. But still I think in the end most people will get bored no matter what becuase the lack of excitement that was felt in the &#039;good old EQ days&#039;.<br /><br />Of course, what do I know&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cwm20.gif" alt="cwm20" border="0" /> </td>
