								&nbsp;<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php#1">General Category</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=10.0">Rants and Raves</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=666.0#msg5790">Re:When a guild loses its identity</a>
							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: February 27, 2004, 12:39:04 am
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Some people will stay with one guild because of loyalty. Some will stay because they like it there. Some will jump from guild to guild because they can never find a place that makes them happy and some will jump to any guild that is higher than the guild they are in at the moment. <br />The reasons for changing guilds are just about as many as the people who do it.<br /><br />As for what happenes when a guild reaches a certain point. Well.. a very few guilds manage to keep true to the path they set on upon creation. Most do not. In order to advance in PoP for instance you need people and gear. In order to get the gear you need a base of people who play and to get the base of people to play you usually have to advance most of the time. &nbsp;That is the killer for a lot of guilds, there are different people who want different things. That is one reason that you will see a lot of guilds splitting at some point or another. <br />If you look at how many guilds on Rodcet that have been around for 4+ years then you will find very very few. <br />The first thing you need to learn in a guild is that you will never ever be able to make everyone happy. It just wont happen. After a while a base usually forms of people who want more or less the same thing and those form the core of what the guild wants. Sometime it works and the guild moves on and prospers. Sometimes it doesn&#039;t work and the factions working against one another are too great and the guild splits or disbands. <br />So there isn&#039;t really any answer to your questions and there are a lot of answers. Funny thing that.</td>
